   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to providing that certain schools to receive tuition\npayments from the state for any period of time such schools are required to\nclose in response to the outbreak of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)",
    "basePrintNo": "S8014",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8014-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8014\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to providing that certain schools to receive tuition\npayments from the state for any period of time such schools are required\nto close in response to the outbreak of coronavirus disease 2019\n(COVID-19)\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill seeks for state to provide tuition payments to 853 schools for\nany period of time such schools are required to close in response to the\noutbreak of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 provides that any 853 school shall continue to receive tuition\npayments from the state for any period of time that they are required to\nclose in response to the outbreak of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-\n19).\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWith the possibility of school closures in response to the coronavirus,\nproviding tuition to 853 schools throughout their closure will help\nensure that they may continue their highly valuable services to meet the\neducational needs of students upon reopening.  During this current state\nof emergency, schools that deem it necessary to close in order to\nprotect their students, faculty, and staff from exposure should not be\nhindered by losing tuition funding.  Through continued provision of\nfunding for 853 schools in these circumstances, this bill can ensure\nthat the state supports these schools to take appropriate action in\nresponse to the coronavirus outbreak.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
