    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8014a\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to providing that certain schools to receive tuition\npayments from the state for any period of time such schools are required\nto close in response to the outbreak of coronavirus disease 2019\n(COVID-19)\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill provides that certain schools to receive tuition payments from\nthe state for any period of time such schools are required to close in\nresponse to the outbreak of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 provides that any 853 school and, any institution set forth\nsection 4201 of the education law providing instruction for the deaf or\nthe blind and any provider of special education services or programs\npursuant to section 4410 of shall continue to receive tuition payments\nfrom the state for any period of time that they are required to close in\nresponse to the outbreak of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19).\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWith the possibility of school closures in response to the coronavirus,\nproviding tuition to non-traditional public schools throughout their\nclosure will help ensure that they may continue their highly valuable\nservices to meet the educational needs of students upon reopening.\nDuring this current state of emergency, schools that deem it necessary\nto close in order to protect their students, faculty, and staff from\nexposure should not be hindered by losing tuition funding. Through\ncontinued provision of funding for 853 schools in these circumstances,\nthis bill can ensure that the state supports these schools to take\nappropriate action in response to the coronavirus outbreak.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
