    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8014C\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to providing that certain schools\nshall experience no financial harm for reduced enrollment or inability\nto operate for the full 180 session days due to the outbreak of corona-\nvirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill provides that certain schools to receive tuition payments from\nthe state for any period of time such schools are required to close in\nresponse to the outbreak of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19)\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 provides that any 853 school, any institution set forth\nsection 4201 of the education law providing instruction for the deaf or\nthe blind, any provider of special education services or programs pursu-\nant to section 4410 of education law and any special act school\ndistrict; shall continue to receive tuition payments from the state for\nany period of time that they are required to close in response to the\noutbreak of coronavirus disease 2019(COVID-19).\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWith the possibility of school closures in response to the coronavirus,\nproviding tuition to non-traditional public schools throughout their\nclosure will help ensure that they may continue their highly valuable\nservices to meet the educational needs of students upon reopening.\nDuring this current state of emergency, schools that deem it necessary\nto close in order to protect their students, faculty, and staff from\nexposure should not be hindered by losing tuition funding. Through\ncontinued provision of funding for non-traditional public schools in\nthese circumstances, this bill can ensure that the state supports these\nschools to take appropriate action in response to the coronavirus\noutbreak.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
